# 1.4: an effect's CC is its amount too. 64 the least, 127 full (as 1.3), under 64 lets go; held by hand it is full
# again, whatever a CC last said. Half time, Freeze, Octave and Drop are switches (no amount)
wait 500
expect view 0
listen
# nothing sent yet: full
expect amt14 127
# Reverb (key 14, CC 104) at 64: held, the least
midi B0 68 40
wait 300
said Reverb
expect pcc 16384
expect amt14 64
# swept up while held: the amount follows, it is still held
midi B0 68 60
wait 100
expect amt14 96
expect pcc 16384
midi B0 68 7F
wait 100
expect amt14 127
midi B0 68 50
wait 100
expect amt14 80
# let go
midi B0 68 00
wait 100
expect pcc 0
# Rise (key 8, CC 28), a move: its amount too
midi B0 1C 50
wait 200
expect amt8 80
expect pcc 256
midi B0 1C 00
wait 100
# Half time (key 2, CC 22): a switch, held all the same (the engine is told the amount and makes nothing of it)
midi B0 16 40
wait 200
expect pcc 4
midi B0 16 00
wait 100
expect pcc 0
# Repeat (key 7, CC 27) at the least by CC, let go; then by hand on PERFORM (w4): full
midi B0 1B 40
wait 200
expect amt7 64
midi B0 1B 00
wait 200
tap SEL
wait 300
expect view 17
key w4 down
wait 300
expect pheld 128
expect amt7 127
key w4 up
wait 300
expect pheld 0
# 1.4: the screen and the link. Reverb by CC at 96 on PERFORM: its band shows a bar, the link says 33 of 64;
# at 127 no bar and nothing listed (a 1.3 frame and a 0); by hand over a CC's part amount, full, no bar
midi B0 68 60
wait 400
expect pbar 1
link hello
wait 700
expect lamt14 33
expect lstatelen 37
midi B0 68 7F
wait 400
expect pbar 0
expect lamt14 64
expect lstatelen 35
midi B0 68 50
wait 300
expect pbar 1
midi B0 68 00
wait 400
expect pbar 0
expect lstatelen 35
